%N A397844 Decimal expansion of log(r)/log(phi), where r is the plastic number and phi is the golden ratio.
%C A397844 Transcendental by the Gelfond-Schneider theorem.
%C A397844 Equals the similarity dimension of the self-similar set with contraction ratios phi^(-2) and phi^(-3), since r^(-2) + r^(-3) = 1.
%H A397844 M. M. E. Somma, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19041208">Discrete Pentagonal Gauge Theory over the Golden Field</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%F A397844 Equals log(A060006)/log(A001622).
%e A397844 0.58435715765740408674636798789931220584471134520450589929839925955171768718874569...
%o A397844 (PARI) default(realprecision, 120); r = polrootsreal(x^3 - x - 1)[1]; digits(floor(log(r)/log((1+sqrt(5))/2) * 10^87)) \\ _Massimo Michele Edoardo Somma_, Aug 20 2026
%Y A397844 Cf. A001622, A060006.
